id: pm-gh1716
title: "GH-1716: pm files and pm docs --add silently replace an existing link's note, and the receipt reports it as a plain change"
description: "GH-1716 (filed 2026-11-12). pm files id --add path=P,note=N2 on a path already linked with a different note silently replaces the earlier note, and pm docs --add does the same. The output reports changed true and mutation_receipt changed_count 1, which also describes adding a new link, so an agent cannot tell that it overwrote another agent's rationale; the first note survives only in history, which pm get does not show. Found during a multi-agent review round, where an orchestrator lost the implementer's notes on two paths and had to revert the writes and use a comment instead. Proposal from the issue: refuse an --add whose path and scope already exist with a different non-empty note with a conflict code (for example link_note_conflict) naming the existing note and offering --replace-note (today's behaviour) or --append-note (joins the notes); keep an identical or note-less repeat an idempotent no-op reporting changed false; and make the receipt distinguish added, note_replaced and unchanged per link, for files and docs and the SDK link operations alike."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,docs,files,"gh:1716",multi-agent
created_at: "2026-11-13T05:59:08.574Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-13T18:02:28.001Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-13T16:34:00.994Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-13T16:34:00.994Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "An --add whose path and scope are linked with a different non-empty note is refused with a link conflict code that names the existing note and keeps it; --note-conflict append joins the notes and --note-conflict replace keeps today's behaviour, each recorded in history as one operation; Repeating an identical --add reports changed false, and receipts distinguish added, note_replaced and unchanged per link for files, docs and the SDK"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "An add on a link stored with a different note is refused under the item lock with linked_artifact_note_conflict (exit 4, nothing written, no history entry); details.conflicts lists path, scope, existing_note and requested_note, and next steps replay the whole invocation with --note-conflict append or replace, carrying its revision guards. New closed-domain flag --note-conflict refuse|replace|append (default refuse; SDK and MCP noteConflict): replace keeps the earlier overwrite, append joins with '; ' and is idempotent. mutation_receipt.link_outcomes reports added, note_added, note_replaced, note_appended or unchanged per requested link; identical and note-less repeats stay no-ops. reviseLinkedNote and LINKED_ARTIFACT_NOTE_CONFLICT_MODES are exported; strict MCP schema 4.25.0; flag lexicon +1 for files and docs."
expected_result: "A conflicting add is refused and keeps the stored note; append joins and replace overwrites, each one history operation; identical repeats report changed false and receipts distinguish added, note_replaced and unchanged"
actual_result: "Verified through the SDK, the CLI and this repository's own tracker: the conflicting add exits 4 with the stored note intact and no history appended, the emitted append retry executes and records one files_add entry, replace reports note_replaced, repeats report unchanged with changed false; the spec fails 5 of 6 cases against the old merge"
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-dj98,related,"2026-11-13T05:59:08.574Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-13T15:48:38.311Z","harness:claude-code","Progress (branch fix/mutation-outcome-honesty): reproduced on the 2026.11.13 build; mergeLinkedArtifactChanges replaced the note of any existing path+scope match whenever the add carried one. Design: one closed-domain flag --note-conflict refuse|replace|append (default refuse; SDK noteConflict, MCP noteConflict) instead of the issue's two booleans, so no mutual-exclusion rule is needed and the files and docs grammar grows by one flag. The refusal is linked_artifact_note_conflict (exit 4), thrown under the item lock before any write; details.conflicts lists path, scope, existing_note and requested_note; next steps replay the whole invocation with --note-conflict append or replace, carrying the revision guards it ran under and withholding the retry when they cannot be spelled. append joins with '; ' and is idempotent when the text is already a segment. mutation_receipt.link_outcomes reports added, note_added, note_replaced, note_appended or unchanged per requested link; a link first added in the same write takes a later note. Fleet census 2026-11-13: pm-web links files without notes and pm-changelog only reads linked paths, so no released caller re-adds a note. pm update --file keeps the first stored entry and never replaces its note, so it cannot lose rationale."
  "2026-11-13T17:10:58.592Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 1 (Codex gpt-6.1-sol xhigh, Greptile): (1) appending a note that itself contains the joiner was not idempotent; the check now looks for the whole requested text as a run of joined segments. (2) link_outcomes described merge steps, so a batch that revised a note and restored it reported note_replaced although nothing was saved; outcomes are now one per link, judged from the pre-write and final notes. (3) outcome paths now use storage's form (backslashes become slashes), so a migration destination spelled with backslashes reports the saved path. (4) a stdin-resolved literal '-' add, glob or remove entry is replayed in keyed form (path=- or pattern=-) so the retry never reads stdin."
  "2026-11-13T18:02:28.001Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 2 (Codex, CodeRabbit): (1) merge identity used raw paths, so a migration destination spelled with backslashes bypassed the refusal and saved a duplicate; migrated adds, stored links, removes and the add/remove ambiguity check now compare storage's path form. (2) a write naming a new link twice under append was not idempotent, because a same-write entry took the later note while the replay appended; entries of one write now apply in order under one rule, so append and replace replays save nothing and refuse rejects a write whose own notes disagree (details.conflicts[].source this_write, with its own message). (3) the conflict retry names the canonical item id, so a shorthand such as discover never replays as a subcommand."
